-- 050: mosaic_volume_metric_view re-created with business metadata (GENERATED by _enrich_metric_view_metadata.py from the
-- live definition + metric_view_metadata/mosaic_volume_metric_view.json). Logic identical to live (asserted). edw_test only.
CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW edw_test.enterprise_analytics.mosaic_volume_metric_view
COMMENT 'MOSAIC VOLUME & ADOPTION - governed replacement for the PowerBI ''Mosaic Volume Report''. One row per finalized exam reading (status Final / Final Addendum, excluded exams removed) from edw_prod.enterprise_analytics.tbl_exam_inventory. Answers: Mosaic adoption (headline KPI = Pct RPCE Reporting: exams read in Mosaic as a share of RPCE exams, including the intentional PowerBI +0.02 business adjustment), drafting and capture adoption, exam / RVU / TBWU volumes, radiologist counts, and the modality KPI tiles (mammo, IR, CT lung screening, US / DEXA capture). Slice by `Final Date`, `Final Week` or `Final Month`; if no period is given use the last complete month. Measures named ''... In Window'' use a rolling window of `days_back` days ending today (default 14; query mosaic_volume_metric_view(N) for N days) - do not also filter Final Date for them. Every Pct measure is a FRACTION 0-1 (0.74 = 74%); never multiply by 100 in SQL, never re-derive a percentage from counts. Practice columns: Team Rolled Up = Provider Practice (the radiologist''s home practice rolled up, PowerBI ''Team Rolled up''); Practice and Team = the radiologist''s own un-rolled local practice; Managing Practice = the practice that owns the exam SITE; Practice (PBI) = the exact PowerBI ''Practice'' slicer value (exam site, coarser). Draftable / Drafted measures here are a simpler volume-report definition than mosaic_draftable_metric_view (no practice-in-program or radiologist-enrolled gate) and will not reconcile line-for-line; use that view for drafting coverage and reasons exams were not drafted. Allocated TBWU is deprecated - do not use. Not migrated by decision: the PowerBI ''Fully Utilizing'' radiologist-threshold rollups, the ''Eligible Exam Count'' family, and Adjusted-Best / Allocated RVU (no source column). Full PowerBI-to-measure mapping: tools/pbi_semantic_extract/mosaic_volume_measure_inventory.md.'
WITH METRICS
LANGUAGE YAML
AS
$$
version: 1.1
source: edw_prod.enterprise_analytics.tbl_exam_inventory
joins:
- name: dim_drafting
  source: edw_prod.enterprise_analytics_ref.drafting_eligible_rpids_vw
  'on': source.RPID_Procedure_Code = dim_drafting.rpid_procedure_code
- name: dim_category
  source: edw_prod.enterprise_analytics_ref.ref_exam_category_lookup_xwalk
  'on': source.RPID_parent_code = dim_category.ParentRpt
- name: dim_enablement
  source: edw_test.enterprise_analytics.dynamics_rad_drafting_enablement_by_npi_vw
  'on': source.reading_provider_npi = dim_enablement.npi
- name: dim_pbi_team
  source: edw_prod.bipa_analytics.presentation_physiciansubspecialty_vw
  'on': source.reading_provider_npi = dim_pbi_team.physician_npi
- name: dim_location
  source: edw_prod.bipa_analytics.location_dim
  'on': source.Hist_Imaging_Site_ID = dim_location.Location_Key
- name: dim_team_rollup
  source: edw_test.enterprise_analytics.tbl_team_rollups
  'on': source.provider_local_practice_name_curr = dim_team_rollup.Team
filter: source.Study_Status_Code IN ('Final', 'Final Addendum') AND source.Exclusion_Reason_Cd = 'N/A'
comment: 'MOSAIC VOLUME & ADOPTION - governed replacement for the PowerBI ''Mosaic Volume Report''. One row per finalized
  exam reading (status Final / Final Addendum, excluded exams removed) from edw_prod.enterprise_analytics.tbl_exam_inventory.
  Answers: Mosaic adoption (headline KPI = Pct RPCE Reporting: exams read in Mosaic as a share of RPCE exams, including the
  intentional PowerBI +0.02 business adjustment), drafting and capture adoption, exam / RVU / TBWU volumes, radiologist counts,
  and the modality KPI tiles (mammo, IR, CT lung screening, US / DEXA capture). Slice by `Final Date`, `Final Week` or `Final
  Month`; if no period is given use the last complete month. Measures named ''... In Window'' use a rolling window of `days_back`
  days ending today (default 14; query mosaic_volume_metric_view(N) for N days) - do not also filter Final Date for them.
  Every Pct measure is a FRACTION 0-1 (0.74 = 74%); never multiply by 100 in SQL, never re-derive a percentage from counts.
  Practice columns: Team Rolled Up = Provider Practice (the radiologist''s home practice rolled up, PowerBI ''Team Rolled
  up''); Practice and Team = the radiologist''s own un-rolled local practice; Managing Practice = the practice that owns the
  exam SITE; Practice (PBI) = the exact PowerBI ''Practice'' slicer value (exam site, coarser). Draftable / Drafted measures
  here are a simpler volume-report definition than mosaic_draftable_metric_view (no practice-in-program or radiologist-enrolled
  gate) and will not reconcile line-for-line; use that view for drafting coverage and reasons exams were not drafted. Allocated
  TBWU is deprecated - do not use. Not migrated by decision: the PowerBI ''Fully Utilizing'' radiologist-threshold rollups,
  the ''Eligible Exam Count'' family, and Adjusted-Best / Allocated RVU (no source column). Full PowerBI-to-measure mapping:
  tools/pbi_semantic_extract/mosaic_volume_measure_inventory.md.'
parameters:
- name: days_back
  data_type: int
  default: 14
dimensions:
- name: Exam Id
  expr: source.exam_id
  comment: Unique ID of one finalized exam reading - the grain of this view (one row per exam reading). Use for drill-through
    or exam-level lookups, not for grouping.
  display_name: Exam ID
  synonyms:
  - exam identifier
  - study id
  - exam record id
- name: NPI
  expr: source.reading_provider_npi
  comment: 10-digit National Provider Identifier of the reading radiologist (e.g. 1234567890). Identifies a radiologist uniquely
    when names repeat; pair with Radiologist Name for display.
  display_name: Radiologist NPI
  synonyms:
  - provider npi
  - rad npi
  - national provider identifier
  - reading radiologist npi
- name: Radiologist Name
  expr: source.reading_provider_name_full
  comment: Full name of the reading radiologist, formatted 'Last, First M' (e.g. 'Taha, Manuel R'). Match partial names with
    ILIKE '%lastname%' and say which radiologist(s) matched.
  display_name: Radiologist Name
  synonyms:
  - radiologist
  - reading radiologist
  - rad name
  - physician name
  - doctor name
- name: Practice
  expr: source.provider_local_practice_name_curr
  comment: 'The reading radiologist''s own local practice (current), un-rolled - the same column as Team. NOT PowerBI ''Practice'':
    for the practice owning the exam site use Managing Practice, or Practice (PBI) for exact PowerBI parity. For the rolled-up
    Provider Practice use Team Rolled Up.'
  display_name: Radiologist Local Practice
  synonyms:
  - Home Practice
  - Reading Practice
  - radiologist practice
  - rad practice
  - reading radiologist practice
- name: Managing Practice
  expr: source.managing_local_practice_name_curr
  comment: Local practice that manages the site where the exam was performed (current), e.g. 'RP Valley', 'RP Phoenix', 'ESR
    Metro Hudson'. The exam-SITE practice (PowerBI 'Practice' concept) and the column drafting-program eligibility keys on.
    Finer than Practice (PBI). For the radiologist's home practice use Team Rolled Up.
  display_name: Managing Practice
  synonyms:
  - site practice
  - exam site practice
  - managing local practice
  - owning practice
- name: Practice (PBI)
  expr: dim_location.Practice_Short_Name
  comment: 'Exact PowerBI Mosaic Volume ''Practice'' slicer value: location practice short name of the exam site, e.g. ''RP
    Arizona'', ''ESR''. Coarser than Managing Practice (RP Arizona = RP Valley + RP Phoenix + RP Sol + RP Sun City + RP SMIL;
    ESR = ESR Metro Hudson + ESR Long Island). Use for PowerBI-parity cuts.'
  display_name: Practice (PowerBI)
  synonyms:
  - powerbi practice
  - pbi practice
  - location practice
  - site practice short name
- name: Modality
  expr: source.exam_Modality_Code
  comment: Imaging modality code of the exam, e.g. 'CT', 'MR', 'US', 'MG' (mammo), 'BD' (bone density / DEXA), 'IR'. Plain
    film / X-ray is 'CR', never 'XR' - a filter on 'XR' matches zero rows.
  display_name: Modality
  synonyms:
  - imaging modality
  - modality code
  - scan type
  - exam modality
- name: RPID Procedure Code
  expr: source.RPID_Procedure_Code
  comment: Radiology Partners standardized procedure code (RPID) of the exam, e.g. 'RPID22' = CT Head without IV contrast.
    Determines drafting-model eligibility (see Drafting Model Category).
  display_name: RPID Procedure Code
  synonyms:
  - procedure code
  - rpid code
  - rpid
  - exam procedure code
- name: RPID Parent Procedure Name
  expr: source.RPID_parent_code_description
  comment: Description of the exam's parent RPID procedure (the grouped procedure family the specific code rolls up to). Exam
    Category is mapped from this parent procedure.
  display_name: Parent Procedure Name
  synonyms:
  - parent exam
  - parent procedure
  - procedure description
  - exam description
- name: Drafting Model Category
  expr: dim_drafting.drafting_model
  comment: 'Mosaic AI drafting model that covers the exam''s procedure, one of 7: CT Abd/Pel, CT Chest, CT Head, CT Spine,
    DEXA Capturable, US Capturable, XR/MSK. Blank = procedure not covered by any current drafting model - NOT the same as
    not drafted.'
  display_name: Drafting Model Category
  synonyms:
  - Drafting Eligibility Category
  - Draftable Category
  - drafting model
  - ai drafting model
  - draft model
- name: Exam Category
  expr: dim_category.Category
  comment: Broad clinical exam category (26 categories covering 969 procedure codes), mapped from the parent procedure. A
    different, wider vocabulary than Drafting Model Category - do not conflate the two.
  display_name: Exam Category
  synonyms:
  - clinical category
  - exam group
  - study category
- name: Source System Code
  expr: source.Source_System_Code
  comment: Reporting / RIS source system the exam came from, e.g. 'rpceMidwest', 'rpceSouthwest' (the two RPCE Clario systems).
    Use Is RPCE Source for the simple RPCE yes/no split.
  display_name: Source System
  synonyms:
  - originating system
  - ris source
  - source system name
- name: Is RPCE Source
  expr: source.Source_System_Code IN ('rpceMidwest', 'rpceSouthwest')
  comment: TRUE when the exam came from one of the two RPCE (Clario) source systems, rpceMidwest or rpceSouthwest - the population
    behind the '% of RPCE' adoption measures. = PowerBI RPCE Exam Flag (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Is RPCE Exam
  synonyms:
  - rpce flag
  - rpce exam flag
  - on rpce
  - clario exam
- name: Reporting Status
  expr: CASE WHEN source.mosaic_draft_flag THEN 'Drafting' WHEN source.mosaic_read_flag THEN 'Reporting' ELSE 'Baseline' END
  comment: 'How the exam was read: ''Drafting'' (Mosaic AI drafted or captured it), ''Reporting'' (read in Mosaic without
    an AI draft) or ''Baseline'' (not read in Mosaic). Same Drafting > Reporting > Baseline vocabulary as the MER pipeline''s
    Period_Type.'
  display_name: Reporting Status
  synonyms:
  - Period Type
  - Exam Stage
  - mosaic usage type
  - read mode
  - mosaic read status
- name: Final Date
  expr: CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE)
  comment: Date the exam report was finalized (signed) - the main date for slicing this view, e.g. `Final Date` >= '2026-09-01'
    AND `Final Date` < '2026-10-01'. The '... In Window' measures use their own rolling window ending today; do not also filter
    Final Date for them.
  display_name: Final Date
  synonyms:
  - finalized date
  - signed date
  - report date
  - exam date
  - read date
  format:
    type: date
    date_format: year_month_day
- name: Final Week
  expr: DATE_TRUNC('WEEK', source.final_datetime)
  comment: Week the exam was finalized, shown as the week-start date (weeks start Monday). Use for weekly adoption and volume
    trends.
  display_name: Final Week
  synonyms:
  - finalized week
  - report week
  - week of exam
  - exam week
  format:
    type: date
    date_format: year_month_day
- name: Final Month
  expr: DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', source.final_datetime)
  comment: Month the exam was finalized, shown as the first day of the month. The default month for adoption / volume trends;
    if no period is given use the last complete month (the current month is partial).
  display_name: Final Month
  synonyms:
  - finalized month
  - report month
  - exam month
  - reporting month
  format:
    type: date
    date_format: year_month_day
- name: Care Setting
  expr: source.care_setting
  comment: 'Patient care setting of the exam: Outpatient, ED, Inpatient, Pre-Admit, Observation, Unknown or Recurring Patient.
    Closest equivalent to PowerBI Place_Of_Service_Name, but the values do not line up 1:1 - treat as a proxy pending confirmation.'
  display_name: Care Setting
  synonyms:
  - place of service
  - patient setting
  - patient class
  - encounter type
- name: VRA Flag
  expr: source.VRA_Flag
  comment: TRUE when the exam was prepped by a Virtual Radiology Assistant (VRA). Stands in for PowerBI's assisted_flag =
    1 AND (VRA name or comm-note timestamp present) - assumed equivalent, since those separate fields are not in the source
    table.
  display_name: VRA Prepped Flag
  synonyms:
  - vra prepped
  - virtual radiology assistant
  - vra assisted
  - assisted exam
- name: AD Group Added Date
  expr: dim_enablement.ad_group_added_date
  comment: 'Date the reading radiologist was added to a Mosaic drafting AD group (drafting enablement pipeline). One date
    per radiologist: the EARLIEST across ANY drafting category, not specific to this exam''s category. Replaces PowerBI''s
    4 per-category ''AD Group XR / CT Head / CT AbdPel / CT Chest Date'' columns.'
  display_name: Drafting AD Group Added Date
  synonyms:
  - ad group date
  - drafting pipeline date
  - added to drafting group
  - drafting onboarding date
  format:
    type: date
    date_format: year_month_day
- name: Training Sent Date
  expr: dim_enablement.training_sent_date
  comment: Date Mosaic drafting training was sent to the reading radiologist, from the Dynamics drafting enablement pipeline
    (one value per radiologist across all drafting categories). Blank = not sent or not in the pipeline.
  display_name: Drafting Training Sent Date
  synonyms:
  - training sent
  - training invite date
  - drafting training sent
- name: Training Completed Date
  expr: dim_enablement.training_completed_date
  comment: Date the reading radiologist completed Mosaic drafting training, from the Dynamics drafting enablement pipeline
    (one value per radiologist across all drafting categories). Blank = not completed or not in the pipeline.
  display_name: Drafting Training Completed Date
  synonyms:
  - training completed
  - training finish date
  - drafting training completed
- name: Rad Drafting Consent
  expr: dim_enablement.mosaic_drafting_consent
  comment: The reading radiologist's Mosaic AI drafting consent status from the Dynamics drafting enablement pipeline (one
    value per radiologist across all drafting categories). Blank = no consent record.
  display_name: Radiologist Drafting Consent
  synonyms:
  - drafting consent
  - rad consent
  - consented to drafting
  - drafting opt in
- name: Rad Drafting Enabled Flag
  expr: dim_enablement.drafting_enabled_flag
  comment: TRUE when the reading radiologist is formally enabled for Mosaic AI drafting (Dynamics enablement pipeline, one
    value per radiologist across categories). = PowerBI 'Drafting Enabled' column (Mosaic Volume). Filter on it for the AD-group-gated
    First Mosaic Drafting Exam Date.
  display_name: Radiologist Drafting Enabled
  synonyms:
  - drafting enabled
  - rad enabled for drafting
  - on drafting
  - enabled for ai drafting
- name: Team
  expr: source.provider_local_practice_name_curr
  comment: The reading radiologist's own local practice / team (current) - identical column to Practice; PowerBI labels it
    'Team' on some pages. Finer than Team Rolled Up (Provider Practice). Not the exam-site practice - see Managing Practice.
  display_name: Radiologist Team
  synonyms:
  - sub team
  - rad team
  - reading team
- name: Team Rolled Up
  expr: dim_team_rollup.Team_Roll_Up
  comment: 'Provider Practice: the reading radiologist''s home practice rolled up to its canonical parent group via the team_rollups
    lookup = PowerBI ''Team Rolled up'' (Mosaic Volume). The default cut for ''by practice / group'' questions. For the practice
    owning the exam site use Managing Practice.'
  display_name: Provider Practice (Team Rolled Up)
  synonyms:
  - provider practice
  - rolled up team
  - practice group
  - radiologist group
  - home practice group
- name: Local Region
  expr: CASE WHEN LOWER(dim_pbi_team.Team) IN ('esr','lfi','jefferson','gli','rai','rp cascade','rp crossroads','jr','drsrp','rp
    east florida','rp north florida','rp palm beach','rp florida west','pra','esrmh garnet','esrmh hackensack','esrmh legacy','esr
    long island','esr metro hudson','seal team','seal legacy','vrad','spec ops reserve') THEN 'Special Operations' WHEN LOWER(dim_pbi_team.Team)
    IN ('adi','adr','crc central','crc nw','crc sw','midstate','neoh','rad alliance','rp kentucky','rp bluegrass','rac','racsw','rpky','rpbg','ra','adr
    legacy','crc','rad alliance legacy','rad alliance northcrest','rp bluegrass legacy') THEN 'Apex' WHEN LOWER(dim_pbi_team.Team)
    IN ('coastal','greensboro','mbb','northside','greensboro canopy','raf','rp florida','rp sandhills','rp south carolina','soar','boca','gr','nra','rasf','mbb
    legacy','mbb phoebe putney','northside radiology','raf east coast','raf panhandle','raf sarasota','raf tampa','raf tele','rasf
    miami','rasf naples','rp florida legacy','rp florida west') THEN 'Genesis' WHEN LOWER(dim_pbi_team.Team) IN ('advanced
    radiology','alaska','cir','desert','gima','rp socal','iam','iamse','mia','mountain','nir','raa','mxc','red rock','rima','rp
    sol','rp sun city','rp chicago','rp forest city','saline valley','rp valley radiologists','svdi','western colorado','wir','rp
    iowa','gsia','svl','mr','dr','nwir','arsc','dr legacy','dr drs','iamse hurley','iam marquette','iam midlands','lakefront
    imaging','mountain legacy','mountain yampa','rp nwir','rp smil','rp socal lakewood','rp socal legacy','rp socal palmdale','rp
    valley','svdi legacy','svdi san ramon','smi','rima','rima california') THEN 'Maverick' WHEN LOWER(dim_pbi_team.Team) IN
    ('access alexandria','ara','br academic','br community','cirpa','community','rp eagle','ebi','gia','lake charles','rp
    borderlands','rp brazosport','rp corpus christi','rp dallas','rp el paso','rp gulf coast','rp houston','rp laredo','rp
    victoria','br','slidell','acc','rpnm','eag','rpep','rpgc','rph','other','exthmc','rp singleton academic','rp singleton
    community','rp singleton','rose','rp north houston','synergy','access lake charles','community laredo','community legacy','community
    victoria','elite','rp borderlands legacy','rp borderlands lovelace','rp helios') THEN 'Trailblazer' ELSE 'Matrix' END
  comment: 'One of 6 fixed regions: Special Operations, Apex, Genesis, Maverick, Trailblazer, Matrix - mapped from the reading
    radiologist''s PowerBI team = PowerBI ''Local'' (Mosaic Volume). Unlisted teams and rads with no team (e.g. vRad) fall
    to Matrix, as in PowerBI. Filter with equality, not LIKE.'
  display_name: Local Region
  synonyms:
  - region
  - local
  - regional bucket
  - local team
- name: Site
  expr: source.Site_Name
  comment: Physical imaging site / location where the exam was performed - finer grain than Managing Practice.
  display_name: Imaging Site
  synonyms:
  - site name
  - facility
  - imaging location
  - exam location
- name: Day Type
  expr: CASE WHEN DAYOFWEEK(source.final_datetime) IN (1, 7) THEN 'Weekend' ELSE 'Weekday' END
  comment: '''Weekday'' (Mon-Fri) or ''Weekend'' (Sat-Sun), based on the date the exam was finalized. Matches PowerBI''s daytype
    column (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Day Type
  synonyms:
  - weekday or weekend
  - weekend flag
  - day of week type
- name: Priority Description
  expr: source.Priority_Name
  comment: Exam priority / urgency level, e.g. 'STAT', 'Routine'. = PowerBI Priority_Description slicer (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Exam Priority
  synonyms:
  - priority
  - stat level
  - exam urgency
  - urgency level
- name: Interventional Flag
  expr: source.exam_interventional_Ind
  comment: Indicates whether the exam is an interventional (procedural) exam. = PowerBI Interventional_Flag slicer (Mosaic
    Volume).
  display_name: Interventional Exam Flag
  synonyms:
  - interventional
  - procedural exam
  - interventional indicator
measures:
- name: Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*)
  comment: Number of finalized exam readings in scope (all exams, Mosaic or not). Slice by Final Date / Final Month. Denominator
    of Pct Mosaic Exams and Pct Drafting Exams. = PowerBI [Total Exam Ct] / [All Exam Ct] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - Total Exams
  - Finalized Exams
  - exam volume
  - number of exams
  - total reads
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Mosaic Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_read_flag)
  comment: Number of exams read (reported) on the Mosaic platform. Slice by Final Date / Final Month. Numerator of Pct Mosaic
    Exams and Pct RPCE Reporting. = PowerBI [Mosaic Exam Ct] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Mosaic Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - Exams On Mosaic
  - Mosaic Volume
  - mosaic reads
  - exams read in mosaic
  - mosaic cases
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct Mosaic Exams
  expr: MEASURE(`Mosaic Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`Exam Count`)
  comment: Share of ALL exams read in Mosaic (Mosaic Exam Count / Exam Count), fraction 0-1, no adjustment. Filter Modality
    etc. for modality cuts. For the headline adoption KPI (share of RPCE exams) use Pct RPCE Reporting. = PowerBI [% Mosaic
    Exams] / [Mosaic Exam %] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Mosaic Share of All Exams
  synonyms:
  - '% mosaic exams'
  - mosaic exam percent
  - share of exams in mosaic
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Drafting Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_draft_flag)
  comment: Number of exams where Mosaic AI pre-populated the report (drafted OR captured), on any procedure - not limited
    to the 7 drafting-model categories (compare Drafted Exam Count). Slice by Final Date. = PowerBI [Mosaic Drafting Ct] (Mosaic
    Volume).
  display_name: Drafting Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - ai drafted exams
  - drafted or captured exams
  - mosaic drafting volume
  - exams with ai draft
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct Drafting Exams
  expr: MEASURE(`Drafting Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`Exam Count`)
  comment: Share of ALL exams AI-drafted or captured (Drafting Exam Count / Exam Count), fraction 0-1. For drafting adoption
    vs RPCE exams use Pct RPCE Drafting; for drafted share of draftable exams use Pct Drafted Of Draftable. = PowerBI [% drafting
    Exams] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Drafting Share of All Exams
  synonyms:
  - '% drafting exams'
  - drafting percent of exams
  - share of exams drafted
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime
    AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: Exams finalized in the last `days_back` days through today (default 14; query mosaic_volume_metric_view(N) for
    N days). Rolling window anchored on today - do not also filter Final Date. = PowerBI [examslast14days] / [examslast7days]
    (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Exam Count (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - exams last 14 days
  - recent exams
  - rolling exam count
  - exams last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Mosaic Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_read_flag AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back
    AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: exams read in Mosaic in the last `days_back` days through today (default 14); numerator of Pct
    Mosaic Exams In Window. = PowerBI [mosaiceamslast14days] / [mosaicexxamslast7days] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Mosaic Exam Count (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - mosaic exams last 14 days
  - recent mosaic exams
  - mosaic exams last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct Mosaic Exams In Window
  expr: MEASURE(`Mosaic Exam Count In Window`) / MEASURE(`Exam Count In Window`)
  comment: Share of exams read in Mosaic over the last `days_back` days through today (default 14; query mosaic_volume_metric_view(N)),
    fraction 0-1. Rolling window - do not also filter Final Date. = PowerBI [% Mosaic Exams Last N Days] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Mosaic Share of Exams (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - '% mosaic last 14 days'
  - recent mosaic percent
  - mosaic share last n days
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Drafting Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_draft_flag AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back
    AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: AI-drafted or captured exams in the last `days_back` days through today (default 14); numerator
    of Pct Drafting In Window. = PowerBI [Draftingexamslat14days] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Drafting Exam Count (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - drafted exams last 14 days
  - recent drafting volume
  - drafting exams last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct Drafting In Window
  expr: MEASURE(`Drafting Exam Count In Window`) / MEASURE(`Exam Count In Window`)
  comment: Share of exams AI-drafted or captured over the last `days_back` days through today (default 14; query mosaic_volume_metric_view(N)),
    fraction 0-1. Rolling window - do not also filter Final Date. = PowerBI [%Draftinglast 14days] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Drafting Share of Exams (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - '% drafting last 14 days'
  - recent drafting percent
  - drafting share last n days
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Estimated RVU
  expr: SUM(source.estimated_wrvu)
  comment: Total estimated work RVUs (billing work units) of exams in scope; RVU is a billing unit, different from TBWU. Slice
    by Final Date. Denominator of Pct Mosaic RVU and Pct Drafting RVU. = PowerBI [wRVU est] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Estimated Work RVUs
  synonyms:
  - wrvu
  - work rvus
  - rvus
  - total rvus
  - estimated wrvu
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Mosaic RVU
  expr: SUM(source.estimated_wrvu) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_read_flag)
  comment: 'Building block: estimated work RVUs of exams read in Mosaic; feeds Pct Mosaic RVU. = PowerBI [rvu_mosaic] / [Mosaicreportingrvu]
    (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Mosaic Work RVUs
  synonyms:
  - rvus read in mosaic
  - mosaic wrvu
  - mosaic rvu volume
- name: Pct Mosaic RVU
  expr: MEASURE(`Mosaic RVU`) / MEASURE(`Estimated RVU`)
  comment: RVU-weighted share of work read in Mosaic (Mosaic RVU / Estimated RVU), fraction 0-1 - the RVU alternative to Pct
    Mosaic Exams; behind PowerBI's exam-count / RVU metric switch (clinicalofmosaicreporting, '% of Mosaic XR') in Mosaic
    Volume.
  display_name: Mosaic Share of RVUs
  synonyms:
  - '% rvus in mosaic'
  - rvu weighted mosaic share
  - mosaic rvu percent
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Drafting RVU
  expr: SUM(source.estimated_wrvu) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_draft_flag)
  comment: 'Building block: estimated work RVUs of AI-drafted or captured exams; feeds Pct Drafting RVU. = PowerBI [rvu_mosaicdrafting]
    (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Drafting Work RVUs
  synonyms:
  - drafted rvus
  - drafting wrvu
  - rvus drafted by ai
- name: Pct Drafting RVU
  expr: MEASURE(`Drafting RVU`) / MEASURE(`Estimated RVU`)
  comment: RVU-weighted share of work AI-drafted or captured (Drafting RVU / Estimated RVU), fraction 0-1 - the RVU alternative
    to Pct Drafting Exams.
  display_name: Drafting Share of RVUs
  synonyms:
  - '% rvus drafted'
  - rvu weighted drafting share
  - drafting rvu percent
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Best RVU
  expr: SUM(source.best_wrvu)
  comment: Total 'best' work RVUs (source best_wrvu, the best available RVU value per exam) for exams in scope - an alternative
    RVU basis to Estimated RVU. = PowerBI [Best] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Best Work RVUs
  synonyms:
  - best wrvu
  - best rvus
  - best available rvu
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: TBWU
  expr: SUM(source.final_TBWU)
  comment: Total workload in TBWU (time-based work units; same unit as RPWU) for exams in scope - the volume TBWU (final_TBWU),
    not the base / unassisted / allocated variants used for efficiency and capacity. Slice by Final Date. = PowerBI [WU] (Mosaic
    Volume).
  display_name: Total TBWU
  synonyms:
  - work units
  - rpwu
  - workload units
  - total work units
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Allocated TBWU
  expr: SUM(source.allocated_tbwu_current)
  comment: DEPRECATED - do not use; not on the dashboard. Sum of allocated TBWU (current variant), which differs from the
    plain allocated variant on 5.0% of rows (-0.44% net); no variant was chosen, so it is kept for lineage only. Use TBWU
    instead.
  display_name: Allocated TBWU (Deprecated)
  synonyms:
  - deprecated allocated work units
  - legacy allocated tbwu
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Estimated RVU In Window
  expr: SUM(CASE WHEN CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE)
    <= CURRENT_DATE THEN source.estimated_wrvu ELSE 0 END)
  comment: Estimated work RVUs of exams finalized in the last `days_back` days through today (default 14; query mosaic_volume_metric_view(N)).
    Rolling window - do not also filter Final Date. Covers PowerBI's Total RVUs (Last 3 / 12 Months) family by choosing N
    (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Estimated Work RVUs (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - rvus last 14 days
  - recent rvus
  - rolling rvus
  - rvus last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: TBWU In Window
  expr: SUM(CASE WHEN CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE)
    <= CURRENT_DATE THEN source.final_TBWU ELSE 0 END)
  comment: TBWU workload of exams finalized in the last `days_back` days through today (default 14; query mosaic_volume_metric_view(N)).
    Rolling window - do not also filter Final Date. Covers PowerBI's Total TBWU (Last 3 / 12 Months) family by choosing N
    (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: TBWU (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - tbwu last 14 days
  - recent work units
  - rolling tbwu
  - tbwu last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: RPCE Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.Source_System_Code IN ('rpceMidwest', 'rpceSouthwest'))
  comment: Number of exams from the two RPCE (Clario) source systems, rpceMidwest and rpceSouthwest - the denominator of the
    '% of RPCE' adoption measures. Slice by Final Date. = PowerBI [RPCEEXAMS] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: RPCE Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - rpce exams
  - clario exams
  - rpce volume
  - rpce cases
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct RPCE Reporting
  expr: MEASURE(`Mosaic Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`RPCE Exam Count`) + 0.02
  comment: 'HEADLINE MOSAIC ADOPTION: exams read in Mosaic as a share of RPCE (Clario) exams, PLUS a fixed +0.02 business
    adjustment (intentional, confirmed with the business owner). Fraction 0-1; report as returned, never re-derive. Slice
    by Final Date / Final Month. = PowerBI [% of RPCE] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Mosaic Adoption (% of RPCE Exams)
  synonyms:
  - adoption
  - adoption rate
  - mosaic adoption
  - '% read in mosaic'
  - usage
  - penetration
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Pct RPCE Drafting
  expr: MEASURE(`Drafting Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`RPCE Exam Count`) + 0.02
  comment: 'Drafting adoption: AI-drafted or captured exams as a share of RPCE (Clario) exams, PLUS the fixed +0.02 business
    adjustment. Fraction 0-1; report as returned, never re-derive. Slice by Final Date / Final Month. = PowerBI [% of RPCE_drafting]
    (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Drafting Adoption (% of RPCE Exams)
  synonyms:
  - drafting adoption
  - draft usage
  - drafting adoption rate
  - '% drafted of rpce'
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Pct RPCE Of All Exams
  expr: MEASURE(`RPCE Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`Exam Count`)
  comment: RPCE (Clario) exams as a share of ALL exams, fraction 0-1. No +0.02 adjustment - a different ratio from Pct RPCE
    Reporting / Drafting (Mosaic or drafting share of RPCE exams); do not confuse them. = PowerBI [RPCE as % of Clinical]
    (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: RPCE Share of All Exams
  synonyms:
  - rpce as % of clinical
  - rpce share
  - rpce penetration of exams
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Distinct Radiologist Count
  expr: COUNT(DISTINCT source.reading_provider_npi)
  comment: Number of distinct reading radiologists (by NPI) with at least one exam in scope. Slice by Final Date / Final Week.
    = PowerBI [Totalproviders_week] when sliced by Final Week (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Radiologist Count
  synonyms:
  - number of radiologists
  - rad count
  - active radiologists
  - radiologists reading
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Mosaic Radiologist Count
  expr: COUNT(DISTINCT source.reading_provider_npi) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_read_flag)
  comment: Number of distinct radiologists with at least one exam read in Mosaic in scope. Numerator of Pct Mosaic Of RPCE
    Radiologists. = PowerBI [# of Mosaic Rads] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Mosaic Radiologist Count
  synonyms:
  - '# of mosaic rads'
  - rads on mosaic
  - mosaic users
  - radiologists using mosaic
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Drafting Radiologist Count
  expr: COUNT(DISTINCT source.reading_provider_npi) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_draft_flag)
  comment: Number of distinct radiologists with at least one AI-drafted or captured exam in scope (not gated on formal drafting
    enablement). = PowerBI [totalradslivedrafting] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Drafting Radiologist Count
  synonyms:
  - rads live on drafting
  - drafting users
  - radiologists using drafting
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: RPCE Radiologist Count
  expr: COUNT(DISTINCT source.reading_provider_npi) FILTER (WHERE source.Source_System_Code IN ('rpceMidwest', 'rpceSouthwest'))
  comment: Number of distinct radiologists with at least one RPCE (Clario) exam in scope; denominator of Pct Mosaic Of RPCE
    Radiologists. = PowerBI [# of RPCE Rads] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: RPCE Radiologist Count
  synonyms:
  - '# of rpce rads'
  - rpce rads
  - radiologists on rpce
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct Mosaic Of RPCE Radiologists
  expr: MEASURE(`Mosaic Radiologist Count`) / MEASURE(`RPCE Radiologist Count`)
  comment: Mosaic Radiologist Count / RPCE Radiologist Count, fraction 0-1 - an unusual ratio (Mosaic rads as a share of RPCE
    rads, not of all rads), kept faithful to PowerBI. The numerator is not restricted to RPCE rads. = PowerBI [% of Rads]
    (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Mosaic Rads as Share of RPCE Rads
  synonyms:
  - '% of rads'
  - radiologist adoption
  - '% of rads on mosaic'
  - rad adoption rate
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: First Mosaic Exam Date
  expr: MIN(CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE)) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_read_flag)
  comment: Earliest date an exam was read in Mosaic within the current filters - group by NPI / Radiologist Name for each
    radiologist's Mosaic go-live date (do not narrow Final Date if you want the true first case). = PowerBI [First Mosaic
    Case] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: First Mosaic Exam Date
  synonyms:
  - mosaic go live date
  - first mosaic case
  - first case date
  - mosaic start date
  format:
    type: date
    date_format: year_month_day
- name: First Mosaic Drafting Exam Date
  expr: MIN(CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE)) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_draft_flag)
  comment: Earliest date an exam was AI-drafted or captured within the current filters - group by radiologist for their first
    draft. Not gated on AD-group status (PowerBI's was); filter Rad Drafting Enabled Flag for the gated version. = PowerBI
    [firstdraft] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: First Mosaic Drafting Exam Date
  synonyms:
  - first draft date
  - drafting go live date
  - first drafted case
  format:
    type: date
    date_format: year_month_day
- name: Last Drafted Exam Date
  expr: MAX(CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE)) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_draft_flag)
  comment: Most recent date an exam was AI-drafted or captured within the current filters; group by radiologist to spot who
    has stopped drafting. = PowerBI [Last Drafted Exam Date] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Last Drafted Exam Date
  synonyms:
  - latest draft date
  - most recent draft
  - last draft case
  format:
    type: date
    date_format: year_month_day
- name: VRA Prepped Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.VRA_Flag)
  comment: 'Building block: exams prepped by a Virtual Radiology Assistant (VRA Flag = TRUE); feeds Pct VRA Prepped Of Exams.
    = PowerBI [VRA Prepped Exams] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: VRA Prepped Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - vra prepped exams
  - vra assisted exams
  - exams prepped by vra
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: VRA Prepped Mosaic Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.VRA_Flag AND source.mosaic_read_flag)
  comment: 'Building block: exams read in Mosaic that were also VRA-prepped; feeds Pct VRA Prepped Of Mosaic Exams. = PowerBI
    [VRA Prepped Mosaic Exams] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: VRA Prepped Mosaic Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - vra prepped mosaic exams
  - mosaic exams prepped by vra
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct VRA Prepped Of Exams
  expr: MEASURE(`VRA Prepped Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`Exam Count`)
  comment: Share of all exams prepped by a Virtual Radiology Assistant (VRA Prepped Exam Count / Exam Count), fraction 0-1.
    = PowerBI [% VRA Prepped of Total Exams] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: VRA Prepped Share of All Exams
  synonyms:
  - '% vra prepped'
  - vra prep rate
  - vra coverage
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Pct VRA Prepped Of Mosaic Exams
  expr: MEASURE(`VRA Prepped Mosaic Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`Mosaic Exam Count`)
  comment: Share of Mosaic-read exams prepped by a Virtual Radiology Assistant (VRA Prepped Mosaic Exam Count / Mosaic Exam
    Count), fraction 0-1. = PowerBI [% VRA Prepped Mosaic Exams] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: VRA Prepped Share of Mosaic Exams
  synonyms:
  - '% vra prepped mosaic'
  - vra prep rate in mosaic
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Draftable Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE dim_drafting.drafting_model IS NOT NULL)
  comment: Exams whose procedure is covered by one of the 7 drafting models (Drafting Model Category set). Simpler than mosaic_draftable_metric_view
    (no practice-in-program / rad-enrolled gate) - won't reconcile line-for-line. Filter Drafting Model Category for one model.
    = PowerBI [EligibleExams] / Draftable family (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Draftable Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - draftable exams
  - drafting eligible exams
  - exams eligible for drafting
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Drafted Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE dim_drafting.drafting_model IS NOT NULL AND source.mosaic_draft_flag)
  comment: 'Building block: draftable exams (in one of the 7 drafting-model categories) that were AI-drafted or captured;
    feeds Pct Drafted Of Draftable. = PowerBI [Total Drafted XR] / [Total Drafted CT] family (Mosaic Volume) - filter Drafting
    Model Category or Modality for one.'
  display_name: Drafted Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - drafted exams
  - ai drafted draftable exams
  - drafted volume
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct Drafted Of Draftable
  expr: MEASURE(`Drafted Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`Draftable Exam Count`)
  comment: Drafted Exam Count / Draftable Exam Count, fraction 0-1 (volume-report definition). Filter Drafting Model Category
    or Modality for one model, e.g. CT Chest. For the governed drafting-coverage KPI and reasons not drafted use mosaic_draftable_metric_view.
    = PowerBI [%Drafted of eligible exams] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Drafted Share of Draftable Exams
  synonyms:
  - '% drafted of draftable'
  - draftable drafted rate
  - '% xr drafted'
  - '% ct drafted'
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Capture Eligible Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE dim_drafting.drafting_model IN ('US Capturable', 'DEXA Capturable'))
  comment: 'Building block: exams in the two capture categories (US Capturable + DEXA Capturable) combined, read in Mosaic
    or not; feeds Pct Capture Read. Filter Modality = ''US'' or ''BD'' for one. = PowerBI [US Capturable] (Mosaic Volume)
    when filtered to Modality = ''US''.'
  display_name: Capture Eligible Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - capture eligible exams
  - capturable exams
  - exams eligible for capture
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Captured Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE dim_drafting.drafting_model IN ('US Capturable', 'DEXA Capturable') AND source.mosaic_draft_flag)
  comment: 'Building block: capture-eligible (US / DEXA) exams that Mosaic captured (AI pre-populated the report); feeds Pct
    Capture Read and Pct RPCE Capture. = PowerBI [MosaicCaptureCt] (Mosaic Volume); filter Modality = ''US'' for [Captured
    US].'
  display_name: Captured Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - captured exams
  - capture reads
  - mosaic capture count
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct Capture Read
  expr: MEASURE(`Captured Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`Capture Eligible Exam Count`)
  comment: 'Capture rate: Captured Exam Count / Capture Eligible Exam Count, fraction 0-1, US and DEXA combined (filter Modality
    = ''US'' or ''BD'' for one). Follows Final Date, not a rolling window. = PowerBI [% Captured] (Mosaic Volume) when filtered
    to US; PowerBI''s ''% Capture Read (Last 14d)'' is a rolling, Mosaic-reads-only variant.'
  display_name: Capture Rate
  synonyms:
  - '% captured'
  - overall capture rate
  - '% capture read'
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Pct RPCE Capture
  expr: MEASURE(`Captured Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`RPCE Exam Count`) + 0.02
  comment: 'Capture adoption: Mosaic-captured (US / DEXA) exams as a share of RPCE (Clario) exams, PLUS the fixed +0.02 business
    adjustment (same convention as Pct RPCE Reporting / Drafting). Fraction 0-1; report as returned. = PowerBI [% of RPCE_capture]
    (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Capture Adoption (% of RPCE Exams)
  synonyms:
  - capture adoption
  - capture usage
  - '% of rpce capture'
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: US Capture Eligible In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'US' AND dim_drafting.drafting_model = 'US Capturable' AND CAST(source.final_datetime
    AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: US exams in the US Capturable category finalized in the last `days_back` days (default 14); denominator
    of Pct US Capture Read In Window. Unlike PowerBI it does not require the exam to be read in Mosaic, so it can run higher.
    = PowerBI [US Capture Eligible (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: US Capture Eligible (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - us capture eligible last 14 days
  - recent capturable ultrasounds
  - us capturable last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: US Capture Read In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'US' AND dim_drafting.drafting_model = 'US Capturable' AND source.mosaic_draft_flag
    AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: capture-eligible US exams that Mosaic captured in the last `days_back` days (default 14); numerator
    of Pct US Capture Read In Window. = PowerBI [US Capture Read (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: US Capture Read (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - us captured last 14 days
  - recent ultrasound captures
  - us capture reads last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct US Capture Read In Window
  expr: MEASURE(`US Capture Read In Window`) / MEASURE(`US Capture Eligible In Window`)
  comment: 'Ultrasound capture rate over the last `days_back` days through today (default 14): US Capture Read In Window /
    US Capture Eligible In Window, fraction 0-1. Denominator includes non-Mosaic reads (PowerBI''s counts Mosaic reads only).
    = PowerBI [% US Capture Read (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: US Capture Rate (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - '% us capture read'
  - ultrasound capture rate
  - us capture percent last 14 days
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: BD Capture Eligible In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'BD' AND dim_drafting.drafting_model = 'DEXA Capturable' AND CAST(source.final_datetime
    AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: bone density (BD / DEXA) exams in the DEXA Capturable category finalized in the last `days_back`
    days (default 14); denominator of Pct BD Capture Read In Window. Does not require a Mosaic read (PowerBI''s does). = PowerBI
    [BD Capture Eligible (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: DEXA Capture Eligible (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - dexa capture eligible last 14 days
  - recent capturable bone density
  - bd capturable last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: BD Capture Read In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'BD' AND dim_drafting.drafting_model = 'DEXA Capturable' AND source.mosaic_draft_flag
    AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: capture-eligible bone density (BD / DEXA) exams that Mosaic captured in the last `days_back` days
    (default 14); numerator of Pct BD Capture Read In Window. = PowerBI [Total DEXA Capture Read] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: DEXA Capture Read (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - dexa captured last 14 days
  - recent bone density captures
  - bd capture reads last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct BD Capture Read In Window
  expr: MEASURE(`BD Capture Read In Window`) / MEASURE(`BD Capture Eligible In Window`)
  comment: 'Bone density (DEXA) capture rate over the last `days_back` days through today (default 14): BD Capture Read In
    Window / BD Capture Eligible In Window, fraction 0-1. Denominator includes non-Mosaic reads. = PowerBI [% BD Capture Read
    (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: DEXA Capture Rate (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - '% bd capture read'
  - dexa capture rate
  - bone density capture rate
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: CA Lung Screener Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'CT' AND source.RPID_Procedure_Code IN ('RPID6891', 'RPID6891-FU',
    'RAD2282', 'RPID6891-WC') AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime
    AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: CT lung cancer screening exams (codes RPID6891, RPID6891-FU, RPID6891-WC, RAD2282) finalized in
    the last `days_back` days (default 14); denominator of Pct CA Lung Screener Read In Mosaic In Window. = PowerBI [Total
    CA Lung Screener Reads by Rad (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Lung Screening Exams (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - lung screener exams last 14 days
  - recent lung cancer screenings
  - ldct screenings last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: CA Lung Screener Mosaic Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'CT' AND source.RPID_Procedure_Code IN ('RPID6891', 'RPID6891-FU',
    'RAD2282', 'RPID6891-WC') AND source.mosaic_read_flag AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back
    AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: CT lung cancer screening exams read in Mosaic in the last `days_back` days (default 14); numerator
    of Pct CA Lung Screener Read In Mosaic In Window. = PowerBI [Total CA Lung Screener Reads in Mosaic (Last 14d)] (Mosaic
    Volume).'
  display_name: Lung Screening Mosaic Exams (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - lung screener mosaic reads last 14 days
  - recent lung screenings read in mosaic
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct CA Lung Screener Read In Mosaic In Window
  expr: MEASURE(`CA Lung Screener Mosaic Exam Count In Window`) / MEASURE(`CA Lung Screener Exam Count In Window`)
  comment: Share of CT lung cancer screening exams read in Mosaic over the last `days_back` days through today (default 14),
    fraction 0-1. Rolling window - do not also filter Final Date. = PowerBI [CA Lung Screener % Reads in Mosaic (last 14d)]
    (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Lung Screening Mosaic Share (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - '% lung screener in mosaic last 14 days'
  - recent lung screening mosaic adoption
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Mammo Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'MG' AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE -
    days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: mammography exams (Modality = ''MG'') finalized in the last `days_back` days (default 14); denominator
    of Pct Mammo Read In Mosaic In Window. PowerBI''s mammo tiles were always window-scoped. = PowerBI [Total Mammo Reads
    by Rad (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Mammo Exams (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - mammo reads last 14 days
  - recent mammograms
  - mammography volume last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Mammo Mosaic Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'MG' AND source.mosaic_read_flag AND CAST(source.final_datetime
    AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: mammography exams (Modality = ''MG'') read in Mosaic in the last `days_back` days (default 14);
    numerator of Pct Mammo Read In Mosaic In Window. = PowerBI [Total Mammo Reads in Mosaic (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Mammo Mosaic Exams (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - mammo reads in mosaic last 14 days
  - recent mammograms read in mosaic
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct Mammo Read In Mosaic In Window
  expr: MEASURE(`Mammo Mosaic Exam Count In Window`) / MEASURE(`Mammo Exam Count In Window`)
  comment: Share of mammography exams read in Mosaic over the last `days_back` days through today (default 14), fraction 0-1.
    Rolling window - do not also filter Final Date. = PowerBI [% Mammo Reads in Mosaic (Last 14d)] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Mammo Mosaic Share (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - '% mammo in mosaic'
  - mammo mosaic adoption
  - mammography mosaic percent
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: IR Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'IR' AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE -
    days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: interventional radiology exams (Modality = ''IR'') finalized in the last `days_back` days (default
    14 = PowerBI''s 2 weeks; other values are a deliberate generalization); denominator of Pct IR In Mosaic In Window. = PowerBI
    [Total IR Cases (Last 2w)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: IR Exams (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - ir cases last 2 weeks
  - recent ir exams
  - interventional volume last n days
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: IR Mosaic Exam Count In Window
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'IR' AND source.mosaic_read_flag AND CAST(source.final_datetime
    AS DATE) >= CURRENT_DATE - days_back AND CAST(source.final_datetime AS DATE) <= CURRENT_DATE)
  comment: 'Building block: interventional radiology exams (Modality = ''IR'') read in Mosaic in the last `days_back` days
    (default 14); numerator of Pct IR In Mosaic In Window. = PowerBI [Total IR in Mosaic (Last 2w)] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: IR Mosaic Exams (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - ir in mosaic last 2 weeks
  - recent ir cases read in mosaic
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct IR In Mosaic In Window
  expr: MEASURE(`IR Mosaic Exam Count In Window`) / MEASURE(`IR Exam Count In Window`)
  comment: Share of interventional radiology exams read in Mosaic over the last `days_back` days through today (default 14
    = 2 weeks), fraction 0-1. = PowerBI [% IR in Mosaic (Last 2w)] / [% Practice IR in Mosaic (Last 2w)] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: IR Mosaic Share (Last N Days)
  synonyms:
  - '% ir in mosaic'
  - ir mosaic adoption
  - interventional mosaic percent
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: Capture Eligible Radiologist Count
  expr: COUNT(DISTINCT source.reading_provider_npi) FILTER (WHERE dim_drafting.drafting_model IN ('US Capturable', 'DEXA Capturable'))
  comment: Number of distinct radiologists who read at least one capture-eligible (US Capturable or DEXA Capturable) exam
    in scope - a plain distinct count. = PowerBI [Eligible Rads for Capture] (Mosaic Volume); filter Modality = 'BD' for [Eligible
    Rads for Capture BD].
  display_name: Capture Eligible Radiologist Count
  synonyms:
  - eligible rads for capture
  - rads with capturable exams
  - capture eligible rads
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Capture Radiologist Count
  expr: COUNT(DISTINCT source.reading_provider_npi) FILTER (WHERE source.mosaic_draft_flag AND dim_drafting.drafting_model
    IN ('US Capturable', 'DEXA Capturable'))
  comment: Number of distinct radiologists with at least one Mosaic-captured (US / DEXA) exam in scope. = PowerBI [Capture
    Live] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Radiologists Live on Capture
  synonyms:
  - capture live
  - rads using capture
  - capture users
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Head CT Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.RPID_Procedure_Code = 'RPID22' AND source.Source_Procedure_Code IS NOT NULL)
  comment: 'Building block: Head CT exams - procedure RPID22 (CT head without IV contrast) with a source procedure code; denominator
    of Pct Head CT RPCE. A single code, narrower than Drafting Model Category ''CT Head''. = PowerBI [Total_headct] (Mosaic
    Volume).'
  display_name: Head CT Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - head ct exams
  - rpid22 exams
  - ct head volume
- name: Head CT RPCE Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.RPID_Procedure_Code = 'RPID22' AND source.Source_Procedure_Code IS NOT NULL AND source.Source_System_Code
    IN ('rpceMidwest', 'rpceSouthwest'))
  comment: 'Building block: Head CT (RPID22) exams from the RPCE (Clario) source systems; numerator of Pct Head CT RPCE. =
    PowerBI [rpce_Ct_head_co] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: Head CT RPCE Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - rpce head ct exams
  - head ct on rpce
- name: Pct Head CT RPCE
  expr: MEASURE(`Head CT RPCE Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`Head CT Exam Count`)
  comment: Share of Head CT (RPID22) exams that come from the RPCE (Clario) systems, fraction 0-1. No +0.02 adjustment - this
    is RPCE coverage of Head CT volume, not Mosaic adoption. = PowerBI [Pct_ct_head_rpce] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: RPCE Share of Head CT Exams
  synonyms:
  - '% head ct on rpce'
  - head ct rpce coverage
  - pct ct head rpce
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: CT Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'CT')
  comment: 'Building block: CT exams (Modality = ''CT''); denominator of Pct CT RPCE. = PowerBI [Total_ct] (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: CT Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - ct exams
  - ct volume
  - total ct
- name: CT RPCE Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'CT' AND source.Source_System_Code IN ('rpceMidwest', 'rpceSouthwest'))
  comment: 'Building block: CT exams (Modality = ''CT'') from the RPCE (Clario) source systems; numerator of Pct CT RPCE.
    Mirrors PowerBI''s RPCE_CT_FLAG column sum (Mosaic Volume).'
  display_name: CT RPCE Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - rpce ct exams
  - ct on rpce
- name: Pct CT RPCE
  expr: MEASURE(`CT RPCE Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`CT Exam Count`)
  comment: Share of CT exams that come from the RPCE (Clario) systems, fraction 0-1. No +0.02 adjustment - RPCE coverage of
    CT volume, not Mosaic adoption. = PowerBI [Pct_ct_rpce] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: RPCE Share of CT Exams
  synonyms:
  - '% ct on rpce'
  - ct rpce coverage
  - pct ct rpce
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: CA Lung Screener Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'CT' AND source.RPID_Procedure_Code IN ('RPID6891', 'RPID6891-FU',
    'RAD2282', 'RPID6891-WC'))
  comment: 'Building block: CT lung cancer screening exams (codes RPID6891, RPID6891-FU, RPID6891-WC, RAD2282) within the
    Final Date filter (not a rolling window); denominator of Pct CA Lung Screener Read In Mosaic.'
  display_name: Lung Screening Exams
  synonyms:
  - lung screener exams
  - lung cancer screenings
  - ldct screenings
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: CA Lung Screener Mosaic Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source.exam_Modality_Code = 'CT' AND source.RPID_Procedure_Code IN ('RPID6891', 'RPID6891-FU',
    'RAD2282', 'RPID6891-WC') AND source.mosaic_read_flag)
  comment: 'Building block: CT lung cancer screening exams read in Mosaic, within the Final Date filter; numerator of Pct
    CA Lung Screener Read In Mosaic.'
  display_name: Lung Screening Mosaic Exams
  synonyms:
  - lung screener mosaic reads
  - lung screenings read in mosaic
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Pct CA Lung Screener Read In Mosaic
  expr: MEASURE(`CA Lung Screener Mosaic Exam Count`) / MEASURE(`CA Lung Screener Exam Count`)
  comment: Share of CT lung cancer screening exams read in Mosaic, fraction 0-1, over the Final Date filter (use the In Window
    version for PowerBI's rolling 14-day tile).
  display_name: Lung Screening Mosaic Share
  synonyms:
  - '% lung screener in mosaic'
  - lung screening mosaic adoption
  format:
    type: percentage
    decimal_places:
      type: max
      places: 2
- name: In Drafting Pipeline Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE dim_enablement.ad_group_added_date IS NOT NULL)
  comment: Exams whose reading radiologist has been added to a Mosaic drafting AD group in any category (AD Group Added Date
    present), regardless of consent, training or enablement status. = PowerBI [In Pipeline Table] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Exams by Radiologists in Drafting Pipeline
  synonyms:
  - in pipeline table
  - drafting pipeline exams
  - exams by onboarding rads
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Drafted But Not Enabled Exam Count
  expr: COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE dim_drafting.drafting_model IS NOT NULL AND source.mosaic_draft_flag AND NOT COALESCE(dim_enablement.drafting_enabled_flag,
    FALSE))
  comment: Draftable exams (7 drafting-model categories only) that were AI-drafted although the reading radiologist is not
    (or no longer) flagged as enabled for drafting - an enablement-data gap signal. Group by Modality / Drafting Model Category
    for PowerBI's breakdown. = PowerBI [Has Drafted But Not On Drafting] (Mosaic Volume).
  display_name: Drafted But Not Enabled Exam Count
  synonyms:
  - has drafted but not on drafting
  - drafted without enablement
  - unenabled drafting exams
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
- name: Drafted But Not Enabled Radiologist Count
  expr: COUNT(DISTINCT source.reading_provider_npi) FILTER (WHERE dim_drafting.drafting_model IS NOT NULL AND source.mosaic_draft_flag
    AND NOT COALESCE(dim_enablement.drafting_enabled_flag, FALSE))
  comment: Number of distinct radiologists with at least one draftable exam AI-drafted while they are not flagged as enabled
    for drafting (same scope as Drafted But Not Enabled Exam Count). = PowerBI [Rads Not On Drafting With Drafted Exams] (Mosaic
    Volume).
  display_name: Radiologists Drafting But Not Enabled
  synonyms:
  - rads not on drafting with drafted exams
  - unenabled drafting rads
  - rads drafting without enablement
  format:
    type: number
    decimal_places:
      type: exact
      places: 0
$$
